  "scope": "# 661dffbdf39a \u2014 proposed strict-threshold extension\n\nAssignment: `review-ce68771fbbf9aaae`; canonical generator SHA-256 `b69551503d76981fef814186d22a507c5dea6541e0ce96f666ca67a9683d7d15`, rule `d006d6b4ed8b`.\nChange: built an opt-in, episode-fixed `1/3`, `1/2`, `2/3` gray-density rule prototype; `1/2` retains exact canonical Racket bytes.\nTooling: built a public exporter and verifier with visible-only content IDs, duplicate rejection, private provenance, and real Racket label replay.\nChecks: **35 focused tests passed, zero failures/skips**; source hashes stayed unchanged during the final run.\nRetained examples: three episodes, each three demos plus four distinct queries; **all 21 labels replayed successfully in Racket**.\nTeaching: a separate one-seed audit leaves exactly the chosen rule among 57 hypotheses per setting; all 12 queries are identified from demonstrations alone.\nRemaining limits: bounded 18/24-cell sampler, one marker color, finite rival families; unchanged production batteries were not run.\nCanonical/reference changes: **none**. Proposed variants remain unapproved; no training admission or shared API change.\nDisposition: routine task-local prototype and tools; the two supplementary ticket outcomes and commands are in `RESULTS.json`.\n",
